  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Water Management for Sustainable Economic Growth</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Armenia):  This activity aligns with the Biden Administration&apos;s Interim National Security Strategic Guidance call to invest in water security to improve lives globally and advance U.S. national interests. Armenia needs to shift to a new, sustainable paradigm for water management and use. Communities across the country are already facing severe water availability issues. The activity will promote sustainable water management and use by improving the country&apos;s analytical tools, supporting governance reforms, and promoting best practices and innovative approaches. .The activity will support the government of Armenia and relevant stakeholders to ensure that water management systems and institutions implement sound, evidence-based policies and practices in an equitable manner. This includes deepening the skills of the Ministry of Environment and other stakeholders to use modern approaches to data gathering and analysis, and support data driven decision-making on water allocation and management..Conservation practices are a key bottleneck to equitable and sustainable access to water. To address this, the activity will demonstrate water conservation technologies in cooperation with the private sector and scientific institutions via small-scale pilot projects. These projects are intended to benefit communities as well as serve as demonstrators for uptake within the private sector. The activity will support the rehabilitation of water infrastructure in communities to increase equitable access to water</narrative>
  </description>
